.TH "RAPTOR-FIT" 1 "2026-10" "RAPTOR Studio" "RAPTOR Studio Manual"
.SH NAME
raptor\-fit \- Turn plain judgements ('one in ten fail by 100, half by 300') into Weibull, lognormal or exponential parameters. No data needed; the fit is only as good as the answers.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBraptor fit\fR [\-h] \-\-law {weibull,lognormal,exponential} [\-\-quantile P=T] [\-\-block NAME] [\-\-repair] [\-f {text,json}]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Turn plain judgements ('one in ten fail by 100, half by 300') into Weibull, lognormal or exponential parameters. No data needed; the fit is only as good as the answers.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-\-law\fR \fI{weibull|lognormal|exponential}\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-quantile\fR \fIP=T\fR
probability=age, repeatable, e.g. 0.1=100
.TP
\fB\-\-block\fR \fINAME\fR
also print the PATH=VALUE changes that give this block the fitted law (for 'raptor set')
.TP
\fB\-\-repair\fR
with \-\-block, the repair law instead of the failure law
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI{text|json}\fR

.SH SEE ALSO
\fBraptor\fR(1)
